# XSH killpg()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.killpg.001
anchor     functions/killpg.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       killpg(pgrp, SIGUSR1) for a group of two child processes returns 0
           and both processes get SIGUSR1 (within 5 s); the test process,
           outside the group, does not.
note       The children are in their own group, made with setpgid() by
           both parent and child to avoid a race.
test       t/001-group.c

assertion  XSH.killpg.002
anchor     functions/killpg.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       killpg() with signal 0 on the caller's own process group returns 0
           without sending anything; killpg() with signal 100000 fails with
           EINVAL.
note       The caller's group under pcexec holds only the test's own
           processes.
test       t/002-null-einval.c

assertion  XSH.killpg.003
anchor     functions/killpg.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       killpg(pgrp, 0) and killpg(pgrp, SIGUSR1), with pgrp the process ID
           of a reaped child that led no group, fail with ESRCH.
test       t/003-esrch.c

assertion  XSH.killpg.004
anchor     functions/killpg.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       A process running as user 65534 that calls killpg() for a group
           whose only member runs as root fails with EPERM, and the member
           does not get the signal.
needs      root
test       t/004-eperm.c
